alley should be chosen and taken from  the panchayat valley and not from the  other provinces to be brought to panshir  and to  run the government in puncher this is  the first option the second is that the  coming and newly reforming government of  the taliban there should be  a stake for the ahmad mussoon his  supporter and also one of the  statement that he made is that that he  is trying to form a government that is  not basically  islamic and he wants to make a  democratic government that is  acceptable and that is the demand of  avranz as he says in the international  community and he doesn't want to  afghanistan be isolated and not  recognized by  international community but one thing to  remember that panchayat valley is  already  enclaved by the taliban forces from four  sides from badakhshan from baghlan  province from kabul  uh  from  kapisa from either side it is enclaved  of the taliban and it is very hard for  ahmad masood and his supporter to  defend as his  father did in 1996 until 2001 and that  situation and now is a little bit  different and it is hard to be resisted  china says it's closely following  developments in afghanistan its foreign  ministry held a news conference earlier  and said most chinese nationals have  safely returned home the government says  it's prepared to work with the taliban  we hope afghanistan can form an  inclusive and open government which  adopts a foreign and domestic policy  that's prudent and moderate we hope  it'll echo the will of the people and  international community  russian president vladimir putin is  warning about the threat of isil in  afghanistan he spoke to central asian  leaders at a virtual summit and  expressed concern that the group was  still active and could gain a foothold  the leaders agreed to coordinate and  secure their borders  iran says it welcomes a peaceful  transfer of power in afghanistan the  foreign ministry spokesman called for  the formation of an inclusive national  government  the occupation was not a solution to  afghanistan's problems the only solution  is to negotiate between all parties to  achieve a comprehensive peace in  afghanistan  we call for respecting the rights of all  nationalities and women and the  preservation of historical places we  welcome the peaceful transfer of power  in afghanistan and the formation of a  comprehensive national government  representing all afghan parties the  taliban is considered a part of the  future of afghanistan

